-- title:
--   Mod-q fibre of the finite flat model has q-power point count
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $p$ and $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ lies in the non-units of $A$, a term $C$ of the core structure `JZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionCore p q A hA` (which packages the fppf sheaves, Hopf algebras over $\mathbb Z$ and point bijections for the $q$-primary Eisenstein torsion of $J_0(p)$, and enters here only as the parameter on which the type of $F$ depends), a term $F$ of `JZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionFFModels p q A hA C`, a natural number $m$, and a proof $hqp$ that $q \neq p$. Among the data of $F$ are, for each level $m$ and each prime $\ell \neq p$, a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra $F.\mathrm{Hff}\,m\,\ell$ over the subring of $\mathbb Q$ of fractions with denominator coprime to $\ell$, whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra homomorphisms correspond, convolution to addition and Galois-equivariantly, to the $q$-power Eisenstein torsion subgroup of $J_0(p)$; and a finite cocommutative Hopf algebra $F.\mathrm{HffBarQ}\,m\,hqp$ over $\mathbb Z/q$ receiving a surjective ring homomorphism from $F.\mathrm{Hff}\,m\,q$ with kernel the ideal generated by $q$. The assertion is that there exists $n \in \mathbb N$ with $\#\bigl(F.\mathrm{HffBarQ}\,m\,hqp \to_{\mathrm{alg}} \overline{\mathbb F_q}\bigr) = q^{n}$, the count being taken over $\mathbb Z/q$-algebra homomorphisms into an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Z/q$, regarded in the type synonym `WithConv` carrying the convolution product (which does not change the cardinality). Since `Nat.card` vanishes on infinite types and $q^n \geq 1$, finiteness and non-emptiness of this set of geometric points are part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre at $q$ of the finite flat model of the $q$-primary Eisenstein torsion is a finite group scheme of $q$-power order, the invariant $\alpha$ of Mazur's analysis of the Eisenstein ideal being its $q$-logarithm. It is used in the construction of the invariants and pinnings recorded by [`ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionInvPins`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionInvPins).
